This is a very interesting game. For once the dystopian post-apocalypse is due to extreme weather conditions (
) and not zombies or a nuclear fallout. The presentation, story-wise, is excellent, with two stories told in tandem;
The dark themes and the final revelations are a bit expected but also shocking. I found the game a bit sluggish, while walking to and fro and when reading/skipping dialogues. I'd like it to be a bit more smooth, but I guess it goes with the general pixel graphic aesthetic. You won't really miss out if you skip this game, but if you take the time to follow the story it may surprise you, even if just a little bit.

Pros:
- Free;
- Nice design of the cards and the game itself;
- Stable servers (at least for me);
- Good AI;
- You can have all the cards using just the money that you achieve in the game (more difficult and slow than using "payed coins", but it is possible).
Cons:
- On ranked games you can't choose who you will play, and sometimes you play with people that have much more experience, ranking and, consequently, much better decks.
9/10

Approximately 10 hours of qualtity gameplay;
Riveting storytelling, consisting of two solid storylines;
Tricky puzzles that sometimes make you feel like a moron when you are forced to look for a solution online (a perfect kind of puzzle for a point & click if you ask me);
Amazing visuals and a great OST.
To sum up:
Brilliant. Definitely Daedalic Entertainment's Magnum Opus.

